# Troubleshooting log

`docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md` is the project's shared memory for bugs that cost real time to diagnose - a
config that breaks a build in a non-obvious way, a platform quirk, a footgun in a dependency. Not every
error belongs there, only the ones a future agent (in this chat or another one) would otherwise
rediscover from scratch.

When you hit one of these and find the fix, **append an entry before ending your turn** — newest entry
at the top, dated, English, with the exact error text or command where it helps. State what broke, why,
and the fix; link to the file with the real fix rather than duplicating code. Read the file's own "How to
use this file" section for the exact shape.

This is versioned documentation (`docs/`), like the rest of the English specification — it follows the
same git rule as everything else in `docs/`: propose the change, Elise commits it.
